Recently use pannadha first remove pannuvom.

HashMap → fast lookup
Doubly Linked List → order maintain

Time: O(1) for get() and put()
Space: O(capacity)

2️⃣ LeetCode #380 — Insert Delete GetRandom O(1)

Medium

class RandomizedSet {

    private ArrayList<Integer> list;
    private HashMap<Integer, Integer> map;
    private Random random;

    public RandomizedSet() {
        list = new ArrayList<>();
        map = new HashMap<>();
        random = new Random();
    }

    public boolean insert(int val) {
        if (map.containsKey(val)) {
            return false;
        }

        map.put(val, list.size());
        list.add(val);

        return true;
    }

    public boolean remove(int val) {
        if (!map.containsKey(val)) {
            return false;
        }

        int index = map.get(val);
        int lastValue = list.get(list.size() - 1);

        list.set(index, lastValue);
        map.put(lastValue, index);

        list.remove(list.size() - 1);
        map.remove(val);

        return true;
    }

    public int getRandom() {
        return list.get(random.nextInt(list.size()));
    }
}
🧠 Main trick

ArrayList → random access O(1)

But middle-la delete panna O(n).

So:

[10, 20, 30, 40]
     ↑ remove 20

Move last element:

[10, 40, 30]

Then last element remove pannina O(1).

Time: O(1) average
Space: O(n)

3️⃣ LeetCode #155 — Min Stack

Medium

class MinStack {

    private Stack<Integer> stack;
    private Stack<Integer> minStack;

    public MinStack() {
        stack = new Stack<>();
        minStack = new Stack<>();
    }

    public void push(int val) {
        stack.push(val);

        if (minStack.isEmpty()) {
            minStack.push(val);
        } else {
            minStack.push(Math.min(val, minStack.peek()));
        }
    }

    public void pop() {
        stack.pop();
        minStack.pop();
    }

    public int top() {
        return stack.peek();
    }

    public int getMin() {
        return minStack.peek();
    }
}
